HST Office: a run in a character style turned regular over a bold paragraph style stays regular (Writer .doc import).

Word combines the toggle properties (bold, italic, strike-through, ...) of the paragraph style and of the run's
character style: the style value is the paragraph style's XOR the character style's. A run's toggle sprm with 0x81
("opposite of the style") or 0x80 ("as the style") refers to that combined value. SwWW8ImplReader::Read_BoldUsw
looked at the character style alone when the run had one, so text in a character style that does not set bold over a
bold Normal style came out bold. s036.doc (Normal style bold, the exercises in the character style res_gen1, bold
turned off on the runs) showed 30 paragraphs bold that Word shows regular; the wider text took an extra line in five
of them and the document 23 pages instead of Word's 22. hst::sw::ww8::ToggleStyleValue now combines both styles; a
run without a character style is unchanged.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_ww8import testToggleBoldOverCharacterStyle (a .doc made by Word 2021, as base64)
